gosh seam 07: A client with no terminal: nothing read, drawn or restored (-N).

For:   REQ1/FWD-5, and REQ10/SHAPE-1's named exception. A session that only holds forwards open
       has no terminal: it must not read the keyboard, draw, or change the terminal's settings,
       and its standard output is not its own to write on.
What:  STMClient asks Gosh::headless() and, when it is so: init does nothing; shutdown restores
       no screen or terminal; the window is taken to be 80 by 24; no first frame is drawn; in
       place of drawing, the client says once on standard error that it is connected; the
       keyboard and the window-size and continue signals are not watched; and the display is
       made without the terminal's description. mosh-client.cc says "mosh: exiting." on
       standard error in place of its line on standard output.
Where: STMClient::init, shutdown, main_init, output_new_frame, main (stmclient.cc); its
       constructor (stmclient.h); the end of main (mosh-client.cc).
Kind:  guards. Lines are added around the core's, and four conditions gain a term; no line of
       the core is moved or re-indented, so that a change upstream to what is guarded still
       applies. (The copy's indentation inside a guard is therefore the core's, not the guard's.)
Needs: 06-main.
From:  the fork's headless changes at mosh-1.4.0-pf.7, where the test was a member of STMClient.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

diff --git a/src/frontend/mosh-client.cc b/src/frontend/mosh-client.cc
index 3c8b1f9..aae614c 100644
--- a/src/frontend/mosh-client.cc
+++ b/src/frontend/mosh-client.cc
@@ -213,7 +213,11 @@ int mosh_client_main( int argc, char* argv[] )
     success = false;
   }
 
+  if ( Gosh::headless() ) {
+    fputs( "mosh: exiting.\n", stderr ); /* (standard output is not ours to write on) */
+  } else {
   printf( "[mosh is exiting.]\n" );
+  }
 
   return !success;
 }
